tel 1.0

base camouflage
import soundness

info   caches: a bounded least-recently-used map, and a single value memoized with a lifetime
detail
    _Camouflage_ provides the two shapes a cache usually takes, so that the decisions every
    hand-rolled cache makes implicitly — when to evict, what to do when two threads want the
    same missing value, and when a cached value is too old to trust — are made by the type.

    An `LruCache` keeps up to a fixed number of keyed entries, evicting the least recently
    used. A `Cache` memoizes one value, optionally for a limited lifetime, and computes it
    under a lock, so concurrent callers share one result rather than stampeding. In both,
    the computation is passed by name and runs only on a miss.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*
    import durationInterfaces.aviationDuration

    val names = LruCache[Int, Text](100)
    names(1)(t"one")          // computes and stores
    names(1)(t"not needed")   // t"one", from the cache

    case class Configuration(port: Int)
    val config: Cache[Configuration] = Cache(300.0*Second)
    config.establish(Configuration(8080))   // computed now, then reused for five minutes
    ```

    The library has a single source set, `camouflage.core`, and everything is exported to
    the `soundness` umbrella.

refer camouflage.LruCache
refer camouflage.Cache

entry .LruCache   a bounded keyed cache which evicts its least recently used entry when full
  detail
      `LruCache[Key, Value](maxSize)` holds up to `maxSize` entries. Applying it with a key
      and a computation, `cache(key)(computation)`, returns the cached value if the key is
      present, and otherwise evaluates the computation, stores its result, and evicts the
      least recently used entries until the cache is within its size again.

      Reading or writing an entry marks it as recent, so the entries that survive are the
      ones the program keeps returning to:

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      val cache = LruCache[Int, Text](4)
      cache(1)(t"one")
      cache(2)(t"two")
      cache(3)(t"three")
      cache(4)(t"four")
      cache(1)(t"ein")    // t"one": a hit, which makes 1 the most recent
      cache(5)(t"five")   // evicts 2, now the least recent
      cache(2)(t"zwei")   // t"zwei": computed again
      ```

      An `LruCache` holds no lock: it is for use by one thread at a time, or behind a lock of
      the caller's.
  refer camouflage.Cache
  entry #apply   the value for a key: the cached one, or the computation's result, stored
      The computation is passed by name and evaluated only on a miss. A hit marks the entry
      as the most recently used; a miss adds it as the most recent and evicts the least
      recent entries beyond the cache's size.
  entry #contains   whether the cache holds a value for a key
      Asks without computing anything and without marking the entry as recent.
  entry #remove   drops a key's entry, if it is present
      For invalidation, when the underlying data has changed and the cached value is known
      to be stale. Removing an absent key does nothing.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      val cache = LruCache[Int, Text](4)
      cache(1)(t"one")
      cache.remove(1)
      cache.contains(1)   // false
      ```

entry .Cache   a single memoized value, computed once under a lock and optionally expiring
  detail
      A `Cache[Value]` holds at most one value. `#establish` returns it, computing it only
      when none is held or the held one has expired. The computation runs under a lock, so
      when several threads ask for a missing or expired value at once, one computes it and
      the rest receive its result: the cache stampede a bare `lazy val` with a timestamp
      cannot prevent.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*
      import durationInterfaces.aviationDuration

      case class Configuration(port: Int)

      val config: Cache[Configuration] = Cache(300.0*Second)

      config.establish(Configuration(8080))   // computed now
      config.establish(Configuration(9090))   // Configuration(8080), until five minutes pass
      ```

      The value's type is given as the expected type, or as a type argument,
      `Cache[Configuration]()`.
  refer camouflage.LruCache
  entry .apply   a cache with a lifetime, or with none, `Cache[Value]()`, which keeps its value forever
      The lifetime is any duration which is `Abstractable across Durations to Long` — an
      aviation `Quantity` of seconds, with `durationInterfaces.aviationDuration` imported,
      for instance — read at millisecond precision. The lifetime is measured from the
      moment the value was last computed, not from when it was last read.
  entry #establish   the cached value, computed by the given block if there is none or it has expired
      The block is passed by name and evaluated only when needed, while the cache's lock is
      held; other callers wait for it and receive the same value.
